# A widening that misses says which type it wanted, and the sentence puts an
# article in front of the name. `int` starts with a vowel and the article was
# `a` on all three engines, because each built the sentence with a format
# string and no engine asked what letter the name begins with. The front end
# has answered this question since `article` was written for the demand
# diagnostics; the runtimes had their own copy of the wording and not of the
# rule.
pub play = print "{("x"):int}"
